[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Checkpoints and Rollback (Part 2 of 3)","textKn":"Checkpoints ಮತ್ತು Rollback (ಭಾಗ 2 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 2 of 3: a checkpointed inventory engine with an idempotency ledger, an atomic precondition, verification and conditional rollback, the four scenarios, crash injection at every boundary, a naive engine, a changed-parameters conflict and six unit tests that are run. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind checkpoints and rollback (a legal-move state machine, durable checkpoints with a version check, leases and fencing tokens, an idempotency ledger, atomic preconditions, conditional rollback, crash injection at every boundary, a SAGA with durable compensation and a hash-chained audit log), not the real software, and one SQLite file plays both the workflow store and the target system in the engine lab, the provider is a table or dictionary, the clock is a number the lab chooses and nothing real is changed, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied, so the labs are our own implementation and the expected outputs were produced by running them. The lesson Part 3 said it had executed its own example, but that file and its output were not supplied, so no figure from it is reused here. The lesson mentions of eventual consistency, SAGA in production and the EU AI Act Article 14 are conceptual or cited and were not run. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 2ನೆಯದು: idempotency ಲೆಡ್ಜರ್, ಪರಮಾಣು ಪೂರ್ವಷರತ್ತು, ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಮತ್ತು ಷರತ್ತಿನ rollback ಇರುವ checkpointed inventory engine, ನಾಲ್ಕು ಸನ್ನಿವೇಶಗಳು, ಪ್ರತಿ ಗಡಿಯಲ್ಲಿ crash ಚುಚ್ಚುವಿಕೆ, ನೈವ್ engine, ಬದಲಾದ-ನಿಯತಾಂಕ conflict ಮತ್ತು ಓಡಿಸಿದ ಆರು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳು. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು checkpoints ಮತ್ತು rollback (ಕಾನೂನುಬದ್ಧ-ಚಲನೆ ಸ್ಥಿತಿ ಯಂತ್ರ, ಆವೃತ್ತಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಇರುವ ಸ್ಥಿರ checkpoints, leases ಮತ್ತು fencing tokens, idempotency ಲೆಡ್ಜರ್, ಪರಮಾಣು ಪೂರ್ವಷರತ್ತುಗಳು, ಷರತ್ತಿನ rollback, ಪ್ರತಿ ಗಡಿಯಲ್ಲಿ crash ಚುಚ್ಚುವಿಕೆ, ಸ್ಥಿರ ಪರಿಹಾರ ಇರುವ SAGA ಮತ್ತು hash-ಸರಪಳಿ ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು engine ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದು SQLite ಫೈಲ್ workflow ಸಂಗ್ರಹ ಮತ್ತು ಗುರಿ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಎರಡನ್ನೂ ಪ್ರತಿನಿಧಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರ ಒಂದು ಟೇಬಲ್ ಅಥವಾ ನಿಘಂಟು, ಗಡಿಯಾರ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಆಯ್ಕೆ ಮಾಡುವ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ಮತ್ತು ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಏನೂ ಬದಲಾಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ ಮತ್ತು ನಿರೀಕ್ಷಿತ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಅನ್ನು ಅವನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ ಪಡೆಯಲಾಗಿದೆ. lesson ನ ಭಾಗ 3 ತನ್ನದೇ ಉದಾಹರಣೆಯನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿದ್ದೇನೆ ಎಂದು ಹೇಳಿತು, ಆದರೆ ಆ ಫೈಲ್ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಅದರ ಯಾವ ಅಂಕಿಯನ್ನೂ ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಮರುಬಳಸಿಲ್ಲ. eventual consistency, ಉತ್ಪಾದನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ SAGA ಮತ್ತು EU AI Act Article 14 ಬಗ್ಗೆ lesson ನ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಗಳು ಪರಿಕಲ್ಪನಾತ್ಮಕ ಅಥವಾ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಓಡಿಸಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Crash After the Side Effect, Before the Checkpoint","textKn":"ಅಡ್ಡ ಪರಿಣಾಮದ ನಂತರ, Checkpoint ಮೊದಲು Crash","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"One Engine, Four Scenarios, Five Crash Points","headingKn":"ಒಂದು Engine, ನಾಲ್ಕು ಸನ್ನಿವೇಶ, ಐದು Crash ಬಿಂದುಗಳು","bodyEn":"The lesson text showed its engine only in fragments, so this part builds one in full. It saves IN_FLIGHT before it acts, applies the change in one transaction that checks the ledger and the starting quantity and version, verifies against the stock, and rolls back with a conditional update. It runs the four lesson scenarios, then crashes the worker at every boundary and resumes with a fresh engine, then runs a naive engine without a ledger for comparison.","bodyKn":"lesson ಪಠ್ಯ ತನ್ನ engine ಅನ್ನು ತುಣುಕುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾತ್ರ ತೋರಿಸಿತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಈ ಭಾಗ ಒಂದನ್ನು ಸಂಪೂರ್ಣವಾಗಿ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಅದು ಕಾರ್ಯ ಮಾಡುವ ಮೊದಲು IN_FLIGHT ಉಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಲೆಡ್ಜರ್ ಮತ್ತು ಆರಂಭಿಕ ಪ್ರಮಾಣ ಹಾಗೂ ಆವೃತ್ತಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುವ ಒಂದು ವಹಿವಾಟಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ಅನ್ವಯಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ದಾಸ್ತಾನಿನ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಷರತ್ತಿನ ನವೀಕರಣದೊಂದಿಗೆ rollback ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ. ಅದು ನಾಲ್ಕು lesson ಸನ್ನಿವೇಶಗಳನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ, ನಂತರ ಪ್ರತಿ ಗಡಿಯಲ್ಲಿ worker ಅನ್ನು crash ಮಾಡಿ ಹೊಸ engine ನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮುಂದುವರಿಸಿ, ನಂತರ ಹೋಲಿಕೆಗೆ ಲೆಡ್ಜರ್ ಇಲ್ಲದ ನೈವ್ engine ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Four Mechanisms","headingKn":"ನಾಲ್ಕು ಕಾರ್ಯವಿಧಾನಗಳು","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">four mechanisms, none a substitute for another</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">IN_FLIGHT</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">intent saved first</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">apply</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">ledger and condition</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">verify</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">read the target</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">rollback</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">only if unchanged</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">four mechanisms, none a substitute for another</text></svg>","captionEn":"Key, precondition, verification and conditional rollback work together.","captionKn":"key, ಪೂರ್ವಷರತ್ತು, ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಮತ್ತು ಷರತ್ತಿನ rollback ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡುತ್ತವೆ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The four scenarios","headingKn":"ನಾಲ್ಕು ಸನ್ನಿವೇಶಗಳು","headers":["Scenario","Result"],"rows":[["clean","COMMITTED, inventory 90, 1 operation"],["crash after the side effect","COMMITTED, inventory 90, still 1 operation"],["wrong expected quantity","ABORTED, inventory 100, 0 operations"],["forced verification failure","ROLLED_BACK, inventory 100"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"cr_2.py","headingEn":"The engine","headingKn":"Engine","descEn":"apply_with checks the ledger and the starting stock in one immediate transaction, verify reads the stock and the operation, rollback restores only when the stock still matches the operation, and run resumes from whatever state is stored.","descKn":"apply_with ಲೆಡ್ಜರ್ ಮತ್ತು ಆರಂಭಿಕ ದಾಸ್ತಾನನ್ನು ಒಂದು immediate ವಹಿವಾಟಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, verify ದಾಸ್ತಾನು ಮತ್ತು operation ಓದುತ್ತದೆ, rollback ದಾಸ್ತಾನು ಇನ್ನೂ operation ಗೆ ಹೊಂದಿದಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ ಮರುಸ್ಥಾಪಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು run ಸಂಗ್ರಹಿಸಿದ ಯಾವುದೇ ಸ್ಥಿತಿಯಿಂದ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class Engine:
    def __init__(self, path):
        self.path = str(path)
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.executescript("""
            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS inventory (product_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, quantity INTEGER NOT NULL, version INTEGER NOT NULL);
            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS workflows (workflow_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, state TEXT NOT NULL, version INTEGER NOT NULL, idem_key TEXT NOT NULL, product_id TEXT NOT NULL,
              expected_qty INTEGER NOT NULL, expected_ver INTEGER NOT NULL, target_qty INTEGER NOT NULL);
            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS checkpoints (workflow_id TEXT NOT NULL, version INTEGER NOT NULL, state TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (workflow_id, version));
            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS operations (idem_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, fp TEXT NOT NULL, status TEXT NOT NULL, product_id TEXT NOT NULL, before_qty INTEGER, after_qty INTEGER, after_ver INTEGER);
            """)

    @contextlib.contextmanager
    def conn(self):
        c = sqlite3.connect(self.path, timeout=10, isolation_level=None)
        try:
            yield c
        finally:
            c.close()

    def seed(self, qty=100, ver=7):
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("INSERT OR REPLACE INTO inventory VALUES ('SKU-1001', ?, ?)", (qty, ver))

    def inventory(self):
        with self.conn() as db:
            return db.execute("SELECT quantity, version FROM inventory WHERE product_id='SKU-1001'").fetchone()

    def external_change(self, new_qty):
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("UPDATE inventory SET quantity=?, version=version+1 WHERE product_id='SKU-1001'", (new_qty,))

    def propose_and_approve(self, wid, expected_qty=100, expected_ver=7, target=90):
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("BEGIN IMMEDIATE")
            db.execute("INSERT INTO workflows VALUES (?,?,0,?,?,?,?,?)", (wid, "APPROVED", wid + ":inventory-adjustment", "SKU-1001", expected_qty, expected_ver, target))
            db.execute("INSERT INTO checkpoints VALUES (?,0,'APPROVED')", (wid,))
            db.execute("COMMIT")

    def wf(self, wid):
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.row_factory = sqlite3.Row
            return dict(db.execute("SELECT * FROM workflows WHERE workflow_id=?", (wid,)).fetchone())

    def history(self, wid):
        with self.conn() as db:
            return db.execute("SELECT version, state FROM checkpoints WHERE workflow_id=? ORDER BY version", (wid,)).fetchall()

    def op_count(self):
        with self.conn() as db:
            return db.execute("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM operations").fetchone()[0]

    def op_status(self, wid):
        with self.conn() as db:
            row = db.execute("SELECT status FROM operations WHERE idem_key=?", (wid + ":inventory-adjustment",)).fetchone()
        return row[0] if row else None

    def transition(self, wid, new_state):
        w = self.wf(wid)
        if new_state not in ALLOWED.get(w["state"], set()):
            raise ValueError(f"{w['state']} -> {new_state} is not allowed")
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("BEGIN IMMEDIATE")
            n = db.execute("UPDATE workflows SET state=?, version=? WHERE workflow_id=? AND version=?", (new_state, w["version"] + 1, wid, w["version"])).rowcount
            if n == 0:
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                raise ValueError("stale workflow version")
            db.execute("INSERT INTO checkpoints VALUES (?,?,?)", (wid, w["version"] + 1, new_state))
            db.execute("COMMIT")

    def apply_with(self, key, params):
        fp = fingerprint(params)
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("BEGIN IMMEDIATE")
            op = db.execute("SELECT fp, status FROM operations WHERE idem_key=?", (key,)).fetchone()
            if op:
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                if op[0] != fp:
                    raise ConflictError("same idempotency key, different parameters")
                return "ALREADY_APPLIED"
            row = db.execute("SELECT quantity, version FROM inventory WHERE product_id=?", (params["product_id"],)).fetchone()
            if row != (params["expected_qty"], params["expected_ver"]):
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                return "PRECONDITION_FAILED"
            n = db.execute("UPDATE inventory SET quantity=?, version=version+1 WHERE product_id=? AND quantity=? AND version=?",
                           (params["target_qty"], params["product_id"], params["expected_qty"], params["expected_ver"])).rowcount
            if n != 1:
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                return "PRECONDITION_FAILED"
            db.execute("INSERT INTO operations VALUES (?,?,'APPLIED',?,?,?,?)", (key, fp, params["product_id"], params["expected_qty"], params["target_qty"], params["expected_ver"] + 1))
            db.execute("COMMIT")
            return "APPLIED"

    def params(self, wid):
        w = self.wf(wid)
        return {k: w[k] for k in ("product_id", "expected_qty", "expected_ver", "target_qty")}

    def apply_action(self, wid):
        return self.apply_with(self.wf(wid)["idem_key"], self.params(wid))

    def verify(self, wid, force_fail=False):
        if force_fail:
            return False
        w = self.wf(wid)
        with self.conn() as db:
            op = db.execute("SELECT status, after_qty, after_ver FROM operations WHERE idem_key=?", (w["idem_key"],)).fetchone()
            inv = db.execute("SELECT quantity, version FROM inventory WHERE product_id=?", (w["product_id"],)).fetchone()
        return op is not None and op[0] == "APPLIED" and inv == (w["target_qty"], op[2])

    def rollback(self, wid):
        w = self.wf(wid)
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("BEGIN IMMEDIATE")
            op = db.execute("SELECT status, before_qty, after_qty, after_ver FROM operations WHERE idem_key=?", (w["idem_key"],)).fetchone()
            if op is not None and op[0] == "ROLLED_BACK":
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                return "ROLLED_BACK"
            if op is None or op[0] != "APPLIED":
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                return "ESCALATE"
            n = db.execute("UPDATE inventory SET quantity=?, version=version+1 WHERE product_id=? AND quantity=? AND version=?", (op[1], w["product_id"], op[2], op[3])).rowcount
            if n != 1:
                db.execute("ROLLBACK")
                return "ESCALATE"
            db.execute("UPDATE operations SET status='ROLLED_BACK' WHERE idem_key=?", (w["idem_key"],))
            db.execute("COMMIT")
            return "ROLLED_BACK"

    def run(self, wid, crash_at=None, force_verify_fail=False, before_rollback=None):
        def maybe(point):
            if crash_at == point:
                raise SimulatedCrash(point)
        while True:
            state = self.wf(wid)["state"]
            if state in ("COMMITTED", "ROLLED_BACK", "ESCALATED", "ABORTED"):
                return state
            if state == "APPROVED":
                self.transition(wid, "IN_FLIGHT")
                maybe("after_in_flight")
            elif state == "IN_FLIGHT":
                r = self.apply_action(wid)
                if r == "PRECONDITION_FAILED":
                    self.transition(wid, "ABORTED")
                    continue
                maybe("after_apply")
                self.transition(wid, "VERIFYING")
                maybe("after_verifying")
            elif state == "VERIFYING":
                self.transition(wid, "COMMITTED" if self.verify(wid, force_verify_fail) else "ROLLBACK_PENDING")
                maybe("after_rollback_pending")
            elif state == "ROLLBACK_PENDING":
                if before_rollback:
                    before_rollback(self)
                    before_rollback = None
                r = self.rollback(wid)
                maybe("after_rollback")
                self.transition(wid, "ROLLED_BACK" if r == "ROLLED_BACK" else "ESCALATED")


class NaiveEngine(Engine):
    """Treats IN_FLIGHT as 'not done yet' and subtracts again: no ledger, no precondition."""

    def apply_action(self, wid):
        with self.conn() as db:
            db.execute("UPDATE inventory SET quantity=quantity-10, version=version+1 WHERE product_id='SKU-1001'")
        return "APPLIED"

    def verify(self, wid, force_fail=False):
        return True"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"cr_2.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() runs the four scenarios, the naive engine, the crash matrix, the key conflict, the conditional rollback and the unit tests.","descKn":"main() ನಾಲ್ಕು ಸನ್ನಿವೇಶ, ನೈವ್ engine, crash ಮ್ಯಾಟ್ರಿಕ್ಸ್, key conflict, ಷರತ್ತಿನ rollback ಮತ್ತು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        section("1. Genuinely running: the four scenarios")
        for name in ("clean", "crash", "precondition", "verify_failure"):
            e, result, crashed = scenario(d, name, f"wf-{name}")
            print(f"Scenario: {name}{' (worker crashed after the side effect, then a fresh engine resumed)' if crashed else ''}")
            print(f"  Result: {result} | Inventory: {Engine(e.path).inventory()[0]} | operations: {Engine(e.path).op_count()}")
            print(f"  History: {Engine(e.path).history(f'wf-{name}')}")
        print("the clean run committed with inventory 90, the crash run ended exactly like it with one operation, the wrong expectation aborted with inventory 100 and no operation, and the forced verification failure rolled back to 100; the verification failure is a test injection and not a real mismatch")

        section("2. Genuinely running: the same crash without a ledger")
        n = NaiveEngine(Path(d) / "naive.db")
        n.seed()
        n.propose_and_approve("wf-naive")
        try:
            n.run("wf-naive", crash_at="after_apply")
        except SimulatedCrash:
            pass
        res = NaiveEngine(n.path).run("wf-naive")
        print("naive result:", res, "| inventory:", n.inventory()[0], "| the approved target was 90")
        print("the naive engine reads IN_FLIGHT as not done and subtracts a second time, which gives 80 instead of 90 and still reports COMMITTED because its verification always says yes; the ledger and the real verification are what prevent this")

        section("3. Genuinely running: crash at every boundary")
        print(f"{'crash point':24} {'path':18} {'final':12} {'inventory':>9} {'operations':>10}")
        for forced in (False, True):
            for point in CRASH_POINTS:
                if not forced and point in ("after_rollback_pending", "after_rollback"):
                    continue
                e = Engine(Path(d) / f"m_{forced}_{point}.db")
                e.seed()
                e.propose_and_approve("w")
                try:
                    e.run("w", crash_at=point, force_verify_fail=forced)
                except SimulatedCrash:
                    pass
                final = Engine(e.path).run("w", force_verify_fail=forced)
                print(f"{point:24} {'verify fails' if forced else 'normal':18} {final:12} {e.inventory()[0]:>9} {e.op_count():>10}")
        print("every crash point recovered to a terminal state with exactly one operation, inventory 90 on the normal path and 100 after a rollback; the first version of this lab escalated at after_rollback because a rollback that had already restored the stock was not recognised on resume, and treating an operation already marked ROLLED_BACK as done fixed it; the lab injects crashes between steps and never inside a SQLite transaction, which SQLite itself makes atomic")

        section("4. Genuinely running: same key, different parameters")
        e = Engine(Path(d) / "key.db")
        e.seed()
        p = {"product_id": "SKU-1001", "expected_qty": 100, "expected_ver": 7, "target_qty": 90}
        print("first call:", e.apply_with("k1", p), "| repeat:", e.apply_with("k1", p))
        try:
            e.apply_with("k1", dict(p, target_qty=50))
        except ConflictError as err:
            print("changed target under the same key:", err)
        print("inventory:", e.inventory()[0], "| operations:", e.op_count())
        print("a repeat is answered from the ledger without touching inventory and a changed parameter is refused, so one key cannot be reused to authorise a different change")

        section("5. Genuinely running: conditional rollback when another workflow got there first")
        e = Engine(Path(d) / "cond.db")
        e.seed()
        e.propose_and_approve("wc")
        result = e.run("wc", force_verify_fail=True, before_rollback=lambda eng: eng.external_change(85))
        print("result:", result, "| inventory:", e.inventory()[0], "| history:", [h[1] for h in e.history("wc")])
        print("another workflow moved inventory from 90 to 85 before the rollback ran, the conditional update matched no row, the workflow escalated and the 85 was left alone; a blind restore to 100 would have erased that change")

    section("6. Genuinely running: the unit tests")
    stream = io.StringIO()
    res = unittest.TextTestRunner(stream=stream, verbosity=0).run(unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromTestCase(EngineTests))
    print(f"ran {res.testsRun} tests | failures {len(res.failures)} | errors {len(res.errors)} | passed {res.wasSuccessful()}")
    print("the tests cover a clean run, a repeated run, a crash and resume, a failed precondition, a rollback and an illegal transition on this lab's own engine, and they are not the lesson's original tests")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
